From: Escapement
Subject: [PATCH] power: axp20x_battery: expose VOLTAGE_NOW and CAPACITY for AXP2101

The pending AXP2101 series exposes only configuration to userspace:
PRESENT, ONLINE, STATUS, CONSTANT_CHARGE_CURRENT_MAX, VOLTAGE_MAX,
CHARGE_TERM_CURRENT. There is no VOLTAGE_NOW and no CAPACITY, so a fully bound
PMIC still cannot answer "how full is the battery" -- which is the one number a
watch needs.

Both values are already in registers the driver touches, and both were measured
on this board before writing this:

    0x34/0x35 = 0x10 0x55 -> 4181 mV   battery voltage, 14 bits, already mV
    0xa4      = 0x64      -> 100 %     state of charge in bits 6:0

Note there is no IIO fallback available here. The AXP20x handler reads voltage
through iio_read_channel_processed_scale(), but drivers/iio/adc/axp20x_adc.c
has no AXP2101 channel map, so for this variant the value comes straight out
of the register instead.

CAPACITY reports -ENODATA when bit 7 (the gauge-valid flag) is clear, rather
than a plausible-looking 0 %. The flag drops while the gauge resets.

Not included: CURRENT_NOW and HEALTH. Neither register is in the AXP2101 map
this driver carries, and guessing at addresses is how a driver reports
confident nonsense.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
@@ -561,6 +561,42 @@
 				      AXP2101_CURRENT_STEP;
 		return 0;
 
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW:
+		/*
+		 * AXP2101_BATT_V_H/L hold the battery voltage as a 14-bit
+		 * value already in millivolts -- measured on this board as
+		 * 0x10 0x55 = 4181 mV. No conversion or IIO channel: this
+		 * variant has no IIO map in mainline, so read the register.
+		 * Power Supply reports microvolts.
+		 */
+		ret = regmap_read(axp20x_batt->regmap, AXP2101_BATT_V_H, &reg);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		val->intval = (reg & 0x3f) << 8;
+
+		ret = regmap_read(axp20x_batt->regmap, AXP2101_BATT_V_H + 1,
+				  &reg);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		val->intval |= reg;
+		val->intval *= 1000;
+		return 0;
+
+	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY:
+		/*
+		 * 7-bit state of charge. Bit 7 is the gauge-valid flag, which
+		 * clears while the gauge is resetting; report that as
+		 * unavailable rather than a bogus 0 %.
+		 */
+		ret = regmap_read(axp20x_batt->regmap,
+				  AXP2101_BATT_PERCENT_DATA, &reg);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		if (!(reg & BIT(7)))
+			return -ENODATA;
+		val->intval = reg & 0x7f;
+		return 0;
+
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
@@ -1000,6 +1036,13 @@
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CONSTANT_CHARGE_CURRENT_MAX,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_MAX,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_TERM_CURRENT,
+	/*
+	 * Escapement: the pending series exposes only configuration here.
+	 * A watch needs the two measurements, and both are already in
+	 * hardware registers the driver reads for other properties.
+	 */
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY,
 };
 
 static enum power_supply_property axp717_battery_props[] = {
